findings:
- finding_id: C1
  title: from_file_or_default swallows ALL errors including parse and permission failures
  weight: 8
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified that from_file_or_default swallows all errors. Config
    tests exist but none specifically test that parse errors or permission errors
    are distinguished from NotFound.
- finding_id: I1
  title: CliError Display leaks internal details to stderr (CWE-209)
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: 'TEA wrote CWE-209 security tests verifying server error Display must
    not leak internal IPs/ports. Reviewer also verified: ''ServerError shows server
    error: please try again later, not the inner string. CWE-209 mitigated.'' However,
    the stderr eprintln path was not specifically flagged.'
- finding_id: I2
  title: "SiemClient.tenant_id uses raw String \u2014 header injection risk (CWE-113)"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: true
  caught_by: tea
  evidence: TEA wrote header injection tests for tenant_id with CRLF. Dev implemented
    CRLF stripping in client.rs:21,27. Reviewer verified CWE-113 mitigation but also
    flagged [LOW] that tenant_id uses raw String instead of TenantId newtype, noting
    it bypasses validated constructor pattern.
- finding_id: I3
  title: Dependencies use direct version strings instead of workspace = true
  weight: 3
  phase_ideal: dev
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase flagged that dependencies use direct version strings instead
    of workspace = true. Reviewer noted keyring as unused but did not audit workspace
    dependency consistency.
- finding_id: I4
  title: "Config token field silently ignored \u2014 secret left on disk"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: reviewer
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: TEA wrote a test for token exclusion from config struct (no token() accessor),
    and reviewer verified config has only api_url and timeout. But no phase flagged
    that serde silently ignores unknown fields like token, leaving secrets on disk
    undetected. The issue is about serde(deny_unknown_fields), not about having a
    token field.
- finding_id: I5
  title: "Vacuously true test \u2014 assertion is None || true"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the vacuously true assertion pattern (is_none() ||
    ...) in tests. TEA wrote config tests but this specific logical flaw was not caught.
- finding_id: I6
  title: "Test with zero assertions \u2014 only checks non-panic"
  weight: 5
  phase_ideal: tea
  caught: false
  caught_by: null
  evidence: No phase identified the zero-assertion test that only checks non-panic
    with 'let _ = config'. TEA wrote config tests but did not flag this pattern.
